1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,345
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,471 --> 00:00:54,305
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,264
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:56,265
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:00:56,390 --> 00:01:01,771
YEONHWARU

6
00:01:43,437 --> 00:01:44,271
Excuse me.

7
00:01:46,190 --> 00:01:48,400
It's my first time here.

8
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:51,737
What's good here?

9
00:01:57,535 --> 00:01:58,869
Hi, Tinky Winky.

10
00:02:00,746 --> 00:02:02,623
I'm not in a great mood today,

11
00:02:02,748 --> 00:02:04,875
so I want to drink alone in peace,

12
00:02:05,668 --> 00:02:07,253
but someone keeps talking to me.

13
00:02:08,712 --> 00:02:12,007
Just ignore him, and he'll take the hint?

14
00:02:21,350 --> 00:02:22,309
Hey, Sang-hun.

15
00:02:23,561 --> 00:02:26,188
Why are there so many
self-absorbed people lately?

16
00:02:26,772 --> 00:02:28,858
I just came to drink alone.

17
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:32,736
And it's my first time here,
so I asked for a recommendation.

18
00:02:32,862 --> 00:02:34,697
But she thinks I'm hitting on her.

19
00:02:34,822 --> 00:02:36,490
Talk about being delusional.

20
00:02:39,493 --> 00:02:41,078
It's so unfair.

21
00:02:44,081 --> 00:02:46,625
Getting rejected before I even tried.

22
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:47,585
You know what?

23
00:02:52,381 --> 00:02:54,174
You're not really my type either.

24
00:02:55,718 --> 00:02:56,886
I doubt you know that.

25
00:03:25,331 --> 00:03:26,790
We haven't even exchanged names.

26
00:03:30,961 --> 00:03:34,214
If I wanted small talk,
I'd take you to a 24-hour café.

27
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:36,175
You get called weird a lot, don't you?

28
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:38,552
-I bet you do, too.
-Not really.

29
00:03:38,677 --> 00:03:41,096
I mostly get, "You're a good kisser."

30
00:03:54,818 --> 00:03:57,112
Who told you that you're a good kisser?

31
00:03:59,281 --> 00:04:00,574
Does that matter right now?

32
00:04:01,325 --> 00:04:02,451
Because you're not.

33
00:04:03,202 --> 00:04:05,245
Where's the rhythm?
It's about give and take.

34
00:04:05,371 --> 00:04:07,623
Oh, I thought you liked it rough.

35
00:04:08,791 --> 00:04:10,000
Okay, got it.

36
00:04:10,751 --> 00:04:12,711
Give and take with some rhythm.

37
00:04:14,797 --> 00:04:16,340
No, let's stop.

38
00:04:21,470 --> 00:04:23,931
I clearly said no.

39
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:32,481
Feeling guilty about your boyfriend?

40
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:34,233
No.

41
00:04:35,109 --> 00:04:37,319
It's just that you suck.

42
00:04:41,031 --> 00:04:42,157
Is this funny?

43
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,617
You're heavy. Get off.

44
00:04:45,577 --> 00:04:46,662
Jeez.

45
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:00,259
You're such a mood killer.

46
00:05:02,511 --> 00:05:04,388
That was fun. It's been a while.

47
00:05:09,184 --> 00:05:10,144
Hey!

48
00:05:14,189 --> 00:05:16,650
Namgung Ho and I first met at age seven.

49
00:05:29,204 --> 00:05:32,666
We've seen each other at our rawest
since we were kids.

50
00:05:32,791 --> 00:05:34,626
"Do you know solitude?"

51
00:05:35,294 --> 00:05:38,797
"I first learned about it
from the movie  Taxi Driver."

52
00:05:39,423 --> 00:05:40,466
"I was nine…"

53
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:48,265
We went through our wild teenage years.

54
00:05:51,101 --> 00:05:52,352
Hey.

55
00:05:52,478 --> 00:05:53,312
What the hell?

56
00:05:53,437 --> 00:05:54,521
-What?
-Why'd you hit me?

57
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:56,148
-I'm sorry.
-Dude, I'm sorry.

58
00:05:56,273 --> 00:05:57,983
-Do you know her?
-What are you doing?

59
00:05:58,108 --> 00:06:00,069
Hey! Oh my god!

60
00:06:00,194 --> 00:06:02,696
We were just friends for a long time,

61
00:06:04,073 --> 00:06:07,493
but we started dating when we turned 26.

62
00:06:08,786 --> 00:06:11,246
And we've been together for ten years.

63
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:13,082
Your place isn't even that big.

64
00:06:13,791 --> 00:06:15,834
It's not hard to walk to the washer

65
00:06:15,959 --> 00:06:17,211
and toss these in.

66
00:06:20,506 --> 00:06:21,924
You never clean up.

67
00:06:25,803 --> 00:06:28,263
You only have one mouth.

68
00:06:29,139 --> 00:06:30,682
Why do you use four cups?

69
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,726
Seriously, I can't.

70
00:06:40,275 --> 00:06:41,318
Hey!

71
00:06:41,443 --> 00:06:42,861
I said to crush the cans.

72
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,614
What am I going to do with you?

73
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:15,936
Hey there, Director Lee.

74
00:07:16,061 --> 00:07:17,729
Why are you so down lately?

75
00:07:21,942 --> 00:07:24,528
Option one, the shoot
got delayed by two months.

76
00:07:24,653 --> 00:07:26,864
Option two, you checked the footage today,

77
00:07:26,989 --> 00:07:28,365
and Song Hae-na's acting sucked.

78
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:31,577
Option three, the studio keeps rejecting
the music director you want.

79
00:07:31,702 --> 00:07:32,703
Or option four.

80
00:07:33,954 --> 00:07:36,206
You're sad we had to stop kissing earlier.

81
00:07:39,376 --> 00:07:40,961
I knew it was option four.

82
00:07:42,171 --> 00:07:45,549
Option five, the shrimp toast
sold out because you were late.

83
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,893
Should I order fried chicken?

84
00:07:58,854 --> 00:08:00,856
Chicken Five, whole chicken combo.

85
00:08:00,981 --> 00:08:03,025
Extra mustard and yogurt garlic sauce.

86
00:08:03,984 --> 00:08:05,777
-And double cheese sticks?
-Okay, deal.

87
00:08:10,782 --> 00:08:13,202
You hated the idea
of CGI snowscapes anyway.

88
00:08:14,161 --> 00:08:17,497
It sucks that the studio
decided without telling you,

89
00:08:18,707 --> 00:08:20,626
but didn't it work out for the best?

90
00:08:21,293 --> 00:08:23,503
Director Lee Mi-do
is known for her mise-en-scène.

91
00:08:23,629 --> 00:08:25,714
Go all out and end this whole thing.

92
00:08:30,928 --> 00:08:32,221
Can I really end it?

93
00:08:34,139 --> 00:08:36,183
Yeah, end it.

94
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:51,406
1. WILL TEN YEARS TOGETHER
END IN MARRIAGE OR A BREAKUP?

95
00:08:53,867 --> 00:08:58,747
NAMGUNG-TUSH

96
00:09:03,418 --> 00:09:04,294
Hey.

97
00:09:06,213 --> 00:09:07,381
Lee Mi-do, wake up.

98
00:09:08,507 --> 00:09:11,843
Okay. I love you, love you, mwah.

99
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:16,265
Me too. I love you, love you, mwah.

100
00:10:02,436 --> 00:10:03,312
Hey!

101
00:10:05,063 --> 00:10:07,399
SWEET DELIGHT FROM GOOD INGREDIENTS

102
00:10:07,524 --> 00:10:11,403
Today, I'll take you behind the scenes
of the movie  Heartless.

103
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:14,614
Oh, Ms. Lee.

104
00:10:16,158 --> 00:10:18,493
What's this?
Didn't you tell her no personal recording?

105
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:20,412
I did mention it to her manager.

106
00:10:20,537 --> 00:10:22,914
-I'm sorry. I'll tell them again.
-You…

107
00:10:23,457 --> 00:10:25,834
Given the genre,
even a prop could be a spoiler.

108
00:10:25,959 --> 00:10:28,378
All staff are prohibited
from personal recording.

109
00:10:28,503 --> 00:10:30,922
Get the video you just took
cleared by production first.

110
00:10:34,092 --> 00:10:36,011
The director seems mad.

111
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:39,514
I'll make sure it gets cleared
so I can upload it.

112
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:40,557
CLEARED!

113
00:10:40,682 --> 00:10:43,268
I'M SO HAPPY TO SHOW YOU
A GLIMPSE OF THE SET!

114
00:10:47,397 --> 00:10:48,982
DIRECTORS CAN'T BE SO AUTHORITARIAN

115
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:50,442
SHE DIDN'T HAVE TO DO THAT

116
00:10:50,567 --> 00:10:51,651
DID YOU SEE HER EYES?

117
00:10:51,777 --> 00:10:55,655
She's the director of the indie film,
After Spring Comes Summer,

118
00:10:55,781 --> 00:10:56,907
starring Gong Ji-seok.

119
00:10:57,574 --> 00:10:58,909
It's  After Spring Comes Winter.

120
00:10:59,576 --> 00:11:01,828
Didn't she win an award
before Bong Joon-ho?

121
00:11:01,953 --> 00:11:04,289
The first Asian female director to win

122
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:06,625
the Short Film Category
in Florence in 2018.

123
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:10,087
Why does the director look so young?
She looks younger than Song Hae-na.

124
00:11:12,631 --> 00:11:14,174
That's a bit of a stretch.

125
00:11:14,299 --> 00:11:15,634
Ah, damn it.

126
00:11:17,344 --> 00:11:19,679
Factory Manager, wait!

127
00:11:22,933 --> 00:11:25,394
I almost broke my back moving those sacks.
You owe me.

128
00:11:26,603 --> 00:11:28,980
You did it yourself.
Why are you whining to me?

129
00:11:29,106 --> 00:11:29,940
Wait.

130
00:11:30,065 --> 00:11:32,192
The other day, wiping the belt…
Where is it?

131
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:33,777
Here, I got hurt here.

132
00:11:33,902 --> 00:11:35,862
Yesterday, washing trays until dawn,
my finger…

133
00:11:35,987 --> 00:11:36,863
Looks fine.

134
00:11:38,073 --> 00:11:39,991
You're right. Why does it look fine?

135
00:11:40,117 --> 00:11:42,494
Just 30 minutes ago,
it looked pretty beat up.

136
00:11:42,619 --> 00:11:44,371
Wow, talk about crazy recovery speed.

137
00:11:44,496 --> 00:11:45,872
I bet you're making a fuss

138
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:48,500
over the fourth sample
of your Spicy SweeTato Chips.

139
00:11:50,335 --> 00:11:52,337
I told you. There isn't much difference.

140
00:11:53,213 --> 00:11:54,381
No, there is.

141
00:11:57,384 --> 00:12:00,846
You see, the slot before the fourth batch
is Ho-Ho Pumpkin Chips,

142
00:12:00,971 --> 00:12:03,890
and since those are dairy-based,
no matter how thoroughly I do CIP,

143
00:12:04,015 --> 00:12:06,601
-there's a risk of cross-contamination.
-So what?

144
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:08,895
Since the fifth batch
is after Ho-Ho Pumpkin Chips,

145
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,230
you want them switched?

146
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:15,861
I told you it's hard
to change schedules at year-end.

147
00:12:15,986 --> 00:12:16,862
You must think

148
00:12:17,612 --> 00:12:21,158
I'll get soft
if you pull something like this.

149
00:12:21,283 --> 00:12:24,327
No, I'm just saving up points.

150
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:29,749
Like Assistant Manager Shin,

151
00:12:29,875 --> 00:12:32,502
I got money to buy you
a bottle of Celint 18-Year-Old.

152
00:12:33,295 --> 00:12:35,505
I'm not sure if I should go that far,

153
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:37,174
and I don't even want to.

154
00:12:37,883 --> 00:12:40,135
Because I absolutely hate being tacky.

155
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:43,305
Still, I'm good with hands-on work.

156
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:45,348
What are you talking about?

157
00:12:45,474 --> 00:12:47,184
And who forced you to do it?

158
00:12:47,309 --> 00:12:49,060
-You voluntarily…
-Wait.

159
00:12:50,145 --> 00:12:51,396
Where did it go?

160
00:12:51,521 --> 00:12:54,191
It was here…
Or was it never here to begin with?

161
00:12:54,316 --> 00:12:55,525
-What?
-Maybe it's at home.

162
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:57,486
-Lost something? What?
-You seen it?

163
00:12:58,153 --> 00:12:59,196
Your conscience.

164
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:01,156
Assistant Manager Gung!

165
00:13:02,324 --> 00:13:04,534
If you worked me to the bone all week,

166
00:13:04,659 --> 00:13:06,703
you should calculate my pay properly.

167
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:09,748
Based on the hourly rate
of my salary excluding bonuses,

168
00:13:09,873 --> 00:13:11,875
three hours a day, four on Thursday.

169
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,251
And I worked after hours.

170
00:13:13,376 --> 00:13:15,712
So if you multiply that by seven…

171
00:13:17,923 --> 00:13:19,716
It's 375,000 won.

172
00:13:19,841 --> 00:13:23,220
Turns out my labor was worth 20,000 won
more than Celint 18-Year-Old, huh?

173
00:13:24,930 --> 00:13:26,681
I sure worked a lot.

174
00:13:29,059 --> 00:13:30,936
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

175
00:13:41,571 --> 00:13:42,489
Ugh.

176
00:13:51,498 --> 00:13:54,292
-How long will you do this?
-Until you give in.

177
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:57,629
How can I change
what the executives already finalized?

178
00:13:57,754 --> 00:13:59,089
Will you take the fall?

179
00:13:59,214 --> 00:14:00,257
You should, sir.

180
00:14:00,382 --> 00:14:02,759
That's why you get paid
two million won more than me.

181
00:14:02,884 --> 00:14:03,969
Really?

182
00:14:04,886 --> 00:14:06,012
Why?

183
00:14:06,137 --> 00:14:07,514
Get lost.

184
00:14:09,099 --> 00:14:10,016
Okay, fine.

185
00:14:10,934 --> 00:14:13,270
I admit there's a slight difference
in sweetness.

186
00:14:13,395 --> 00:14:14,854
But looking at the internal survey,

187
00:14:14,980 --> 00:14:17,482
feedback is consistent
from the first batch to the fourth.

188
00:14:17,607 --> 00:14:20,652
It means there's no statistically
significant difference.

189
00:14:21,653 --> 00:14:23,989
These are the comments
from the latest internal survey.

190
00:14:24,114 --> 00:14:25,782
Take a look. Here.

191
00:14:29,035 --> 00:14:30,328
SPICY SWEETATO CHIPS
INTERNAL SURVEY RESULTS

192
00:14:33,456 --> 00:14:36,459
The sweet potato flavor is missing,
and the aftertaste is the worst.

193
00:14:36,585 --> 00:14:38,128
It'll flop before it even launches.

194
00:14:38,253 --> 00:14:39,921
-What?
-My condolences in advance.

195
00:14:40,046 --> 00:14:41,965
You wrote this?
It's exactly what you said.

196
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:43,425
I know, right?

197
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:46,344
At first, even I thought,
"Did I sabotage us while drunk?"

198
00:14:49,431 --> 00:14:51,975
I think you forgot
because you're getting older,

199
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:54,477
but something similar happened
with Hot Chocolate Chips.

200
00:14:54,603 --> 00:14:56,688
The person
who caught the steam input error…

201
00:14:57,772 --> 00:14:59,566
I hate to say this myself,

202
00:15:00,275 --> 00:15:01,318
but that was me.

203
00:15:01,985 --> 00:15:03,028
Whoa.

204
00:15:03,153 --> 00:15:06,906
I can't believe I'm hearing
the Hot Chocolate Chips origin story.

205
00:15:07,032 --> 00:15:08,325
It's an honor.

206
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:09,409
Baek up.

207
00:15:16,333 --> 00:15:18,918
I worked all week
to change the factory schedule,

208
00:15:20,253 --> 00:15:21,880
and it was all for nothing.

209
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:25,592
Fine, the first week of November.
No more delays.

210
00:15:25,717 --> 00:15:28,637
Ugh. Get off! Hey!

211
00:15:28,762 --> 00:15:29,971
Hold on a second.

212
00:15:30,555 --> 00:15:31,556
YEONHUI-DONG TWIN FISTS

213
00:15:31,681 --> 00:15:33,016
Get back to work, guys.

214
00:15:33,141 --> 00:15:35,977
-I'll be right back.
-What a pain.

215
00:15:36,102 --> 00:15:38,188
QUEENS HAIR SALON

216
00:15:38,313 --> 00:15:39,731
Wow, looks delicious.

217
00:15:39,856 --> 00:15:40,774
Just as I expected.

218
00:15:49,074 --> 00:15:50,700
-The spinach is amazing.
-I know.

219
00:15:54,454 --> 00:15:55,497
You two.

220
00:15:56,790 --> 00:15:57,916
Decide right now.

221
00:15:58,792 --> 00:16:01,670
Whether you're getting married
or breaking up.

222
00:16:02,379 --> 00:16:03,213
Choose.

223
00:16:05,882 --> 00:16:08,134
Jeez, Mom, are you crazy?

224
00:16:08,259 --> 00:16:11,763
He has a permanent corporate job,
a great salary, and solid benefits.

225
00:16:11,888 --> 00:16:13,890
Why would Namgung settle

226
00:16:14,015 --> 00:16:15,558
for a girl with no stability?

227
00:16:16,559 --> 00:16:17,852
That doesn't make any sense.

228
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:21,314
He's like a brother to me.
I don't want him to be unhappy either.

229
00:16:23,233 --> 00:16:24,150
It's true, Mom!

230
00:16:33,118 --> 00:16:33,952
Ho.

231
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:36,871
Don't let her fool you anymore.

232
00:16:40,375 --> 00:16:43,002
Yes, Gang Dong-won is in.
We have Chinese investors too.

233
00:16:43,128 --> 00:16:44,087
29-YEAR-OLD LEE MI-DO

234
00:16:44,212 --> 00:16:46,005
I think it'll happen faster than expected.

235
00:16:46,131 --> 00:16:48,717
Anyway, Mom, just keep looking
for an apartment.

236
00:16:50,802 --> 00:16:52,595
Gong Yoo is confirmed.

237
00:16:52,721 --> 00:16:54,139
He's split between a drama and a movie…

238
00:16:54,264 --> 00:16:55,098
30-YEAR-OLD LEE MI-DO

239
00:16:55,223 --> 00:16:57,434
…but he'll seal the deal next week
once it's decided.

240
00:16:57,559 --> 00:17:01,396
So just keep looking
for an apartment, okay?

241
00:17:01,521 --> 00:17:02,605
It's not my fault!

242
00:17:02,731 --> 00:17:05,483
You think I wanted this?
Is it my fault the studio went under?

243
00:17:05,608 --> 00:17:06,526
32-YEAR-OLD LEE MI-DO

244
00:17:06,651 --> 00:17:07,485
Whatever.

245
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:09,237
It was just
a small price to pay for this film.

246
00:17:10,238 --> 00:17:12,115
This time it's for real.

247
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:14,159
Keep looking for a nice apartment.

248
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:17,495
33-YEAR-OLD LEE MI-DO

249
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:20,081
The investors' response isn't bad,

250
00:17:20,999 --> 00:17:22,625
so for real this time…

251
00:17:24,127 --> 00:17:25,837
It's not 100% certain yet.

252
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:28,506
Still, keep looking for an apart--

253
00:17:32,469 --> 00:17:34,721
Come on, Ms. Ma. Why bring up the past…

254
00:17:38,349 --> 00:17:40,351
Actually, you do have a point.

255
00:17:40,477 --> 00:17:42,479
She says it out of love, so you…

256
00:17:43,855 --> 00:17:45,440
Just ignore it.

257
00:17:49,277 --> 00:17:50,278
Here.

258
00:17:50,904 --> 00:17:54,199
Ms. Ma, you saw all the articles
about Mi-do's movie.

259
00:17:54,324 --> 00:17:56,493
It's for real this time.

260
00:18:00,121 --> 00:18:02,582
Yes, Mom, I saw it too.

261
00:18:02,707 --> 00:18:04,501
Song Hae-na posted it online.

262
00:18:04,626 --> 00:18:05,585
-Right.
-Yes.

263
00:18:05,710 --> 00:18:08,046
Making a movie
doesn't guarantee anything, though.

264
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:12,217
Mom, so many movies these days
never even get released.

265
00:18:12,342 --> 00:18:13,426
What a shame.

266
00:18:17,597 --> 00:18:19,808
Anyway, it's really certain this time.

267
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:22,602
Lee Mi-do only gets picked on here.

268
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:25,021
Out there, she's a respected director.

269
00:18:25,146 --> 00:18:26,189
Enough.

270
00:18:27,398 --> 00:18:28,983
You two promised, right?

271
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:32,070
That you'd get married
once she becomes a director.

272
00:18:32,737 --> 00:18:35,073
I'll give you six months. Do it by then.

273
00:18:39,702 --> 00:18:41,788
But six months is…

274
00:18:41,913 --> 00:18:45,959
Well, Mi-do's filming got delayed
because of the snowy mountain scene,

275
00:18:46,084 --> 00:18:47,085
and the editing--

276
00:18:47,210 --> 00:18:49,504
If you factor all that in, when will you?

277
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:51,381
Whether the movie succeeds or fails,

278
00:18:51,506 --> 00:18:52,382
you'll say no.

279
00:18:52,507 --> 00:18:54,300
You're just making excuses.

280
00:18:56,970 --> 00:19:00,098
Look at her.
I just said a few words, and look.

281
00:19:00,223 --> 00:19:01,057
That temper.

282
00:19:01,182 --> 00:19:02,559
Do you have anything for indigestion?

283
00:19:03,434 --> 00:19:05,520
Stomach issues again? Are you okay?

284
00:19:09,065 --> 00:19:10,525
Hey, are you maybe…

285
00:19:11,317 --> 00:19:12,402
No.

286
00:19:12,527 --> 00:19:14,487
Just in case, don't take any medicine.

287
00:19:14,612 --> 00:19:15,989
I said no, period.

288
00:19:16,114 --> 00:19:18,074
How would you know?

289
00:19:18,199 --> 00:19:19,701
It never hurts to be careful.

290
00:19:19,826 --> 00:19:21,619
We haven't done it in six months.

291
00:19:29,085 --> 00:19:31,754
Hey, are you out of your mind?

292
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:33,840
Why say that in front of your mom?

293
00:19:34,799 --> 00:19:35,800
If I hadn't,

294
00:19:35,925 --> 00:19:39,429
we'd be deciding whether to go
to Guam or Cebu for our honeymoon.

295
00:19:39,554 --> 00:19:41,264
You should be thanking me.

296
00:19:41,389 --> 00:19:42,640
"Oh, really?"

297
00:19:42,765 --> 00:19:45,435
"How thoughtful."
Did you think I'd say that?

298
00:19:47,145 --> 00:19:48,730
Honestly, I'm right, aren't I?

299
00:19:48,855 --> 00:19:49,939
Hey, that's…

300
00:19:52,025 --> 00:19:53,860
We've both been busy lately, so…

301
00:19:58,323 --> 00:19:59,699
Has it been that long?

302
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:01,743
It was around…

303
00:20:01,868 --> 00:20:03,703
Hey, don't count.

304
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:05,663
Right. I guess so.

305
00:20:07,373 --> 00:20:09,208
I told you we shouldn't go.

306
00:20:09,334 --> 00:20:11,753
She always does that
around this time of year.

307
00:20:12,962 --> 00:20:15,840
She's just doing that
because she's worried about you.

308
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:23,056
It's just delayed because of your film.

309
00:20:24,432 --> 00:20:26,309
We've thought about getting married.

310
00:20:29,270 --> 00:20:31,606
So what, you actually want to get married?

311
00:20:31,731 --> 00:20:34,025
Yes, I want to.

312
00:20:37,862 --> 00:20:38,821
You don't want to?

313
00:20:47,205 --> 00:20:49,958
It's not that I don't want to.
I'm just scared.

314
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,293
I mean, marriage

315
00:20:52,418 --> 00:20:55,797
is ending the second act of life
and entering the third act,

316
00:20:55,922 --> 00:20:58,132
and I haven't even done
my second act right.

317
00:20:59,592 --> 00:21:02,595
I mean, sure,
I'm shooting a movie right now,

318
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:04,639
but I don't know how it'll turn out.

319
00:21:12,981 --> 00:21:14,357
I know myself.

320
00:21:16,317 --> 00:21:18,486
I'm selfish and self-centered.

321
00:21:19,362 --> 00:21:21,030
If I marry you,

322
00:21:21,155 --> 00:21:24,033
I'd probably settle into the comfort
and security you provide,

323
00:21:25,368 --> 00:21:27,829
stop writing, and leech off of you.

324
00:21:27,954 --> 00:21:29,622
But I can't do that.

325
00:21:29,747 --> 00:21:31,749
That would just be the absolute worst.

326
00:21:32,375 --> 00:21:35,461
Then was I leeching off of you back then?

327
00:21:35,586 --> 00:21:36,587
Hey.

328
00:21:36,713 --> 00:21:38,089
My point, exactly.

329
00:21:39,382 --> 00:21:40,800
Why call it "leeching off"?

330
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:43,886
Reliance, coexistence, care.
Use better words.

331
00:21:44,012 --> 00:21:45,013
No, I mean…

332
00:21:46,597 --> 00:21:48,349
Drink up. You said your stomach's upset.

333
00:21:53,896 --> 00:21:55,857
I have leftover abalone. Is porridge okay?

334
00:21:56,524 --> 00:21:58,985
You were just
picking at your food earlier.

335
00:22:06,617 --> 00:22:08,619
I don't want porridge. Make fried rice.

336
00:22:08,745 --> 00:22:11,372
You have an upset stomach.
Just eat the porridge.

337
00:22:16,753 --> 00:22:18,171
Do you remember that time?

338
00:22:20,214 --> 00:22:22,341
During summer break in ninth grade.

339
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:33,603
EMERGENCY ROOM

340
00:22:33,728 --> 00:22:35,480
Come. This way.

341
00:22:36,272 --> 00:22:38,441
I was running with you on my back,

342
00:22:39,150 --> 00:22:41,402
and you didn't feel heavy at all.

343
00:22:41,527 --> 00:22:42,945
Lee Mi-do! Lee Mi-do!

344
00:22:47,241 --> 00:22:48,076
Blood test.

345
00:22:48,201 --> 00:22:49,327
Yes, Doctor.

346
00:22:49,994 --> 00:22:51,162
I'll check your temperature.

347
00:22:52,997 --> 00:22:54,624
And I found out later.

348
00:22:56,292 --> 00:23:00,171
I had carried you ten kilometers
in just 30 minutes.

349
00:23:03,341 --> 00:23:05,843
So don't talk about leeching off of me.

350
00:23:06,511 --> 00:23:08,346
With you on my back…

351
00:23:10,556 --> 00:23:11,808
I get stronger.

352
00:23:15,061 --> 00:23:15,978
I always have.

353
00:23:17,105 --> 00:23:19,607
I guess you're like an energy booster.
Something like that.

354
00:23:25,488 --> 00:23:27,448
My movie might flop.

355
00:23:27,573 --> 00:23:28,991
-Is that okay?
-Yeah.

356
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:31,994
Even if I cling to you
and do nothing but breathe forever?

357
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:33,496
Yeah, it can flop.

358
00:23:33,621 --> 00:23:34,705
If I kill someone?

359
00:23:34,831 --> 00:23:36,415
Hey.

360
00:23:37,083 --> 00:23:38,751
I'm trying to be serious here.

361
00:23:38,876 --> 00:23:40,211
Answer me.

362
00:23:45,716 --> 00:23:46,634
Well…

363
00:23:48,094 --> 00:23:49,512
I'd probably curse you out.

364
00:23:51,222 --> 00:23:52,348
A whole lot.

365
00:24:00,314 --> 00:24:02,400
But I'd bring you care packages in prison.

366
00:24:09,657 --> 00:24:10,491
Carrots.

367
00:24:11,325 --> 00:24:13,327
Cut them smaller. I hate chunks.

368
00:24:14,036 --> 00:24:15,037
Yes, ma'am.

369
00:24:31,345 --> 00:24:32,597
Why are you awake?

370
00:24:35,516 --> 00:24:36,434
Namgung.

371
00:24:38,728 --> 00:24:41,272
Is it really okay if my movie flops?

372
00:24:49,822 --> 00:24:51,073
It's okay.

373
00:24:52,491 --> 00:24:53,951
It's totally fine.

374
00:24:55,119 --> 00:24:57,705
Just do your best with no regrets.

375
00:24:59,707 --> 00:25:01,167
That's all you need to do.

376
00:25:30,029 --> 00:25:31,614
Cut! Let's take a short break.

377
00:25:31,739 --> 00:25:32,990
We're taking a break.

378
00:25:38,329 --> 00:25:40,122
24 HOURS IS NEVER ENOUGH

379
00:25:42,124 --> 00:25:43,084
I'm so sorry.

380
00:25:43,209 --> 00:25:45,127
I've never done this genre before.

381
00:25:47,129 --> 00:25:50,633
I actually debuted in
Director Hwang Seung-ki's  Manifesto.

382
00:25:50,758 --> 00:25:51,968
I was a rising star,

383
00:25:52,093 --> 00:25:53,886
doing all kinds of TV shows…

384
00:25:54,011 --> 00:25:55,721
Oh, man. You don't know.

385
00:25:57,223 --> 00:25:59,684
D flat? Or E?

386
00:26:01,310 --> 00:26:02,144
Come again?

387
00:26:02,270 --> 00:26:04,563
Ah, ah, ah.

388
00:26:04,689 --> 00:26:06,232
Ah. Around this pitch.

389
00:26:06,357 --> 00:26:07,441
Can you do that?

390
00:26:08,150 --> 00:26:11,070
-Ah, ah, ah.
-Yes.

391
00:26:11,195 --> 00:26:13,823
If the guy moans
at a higher pitch than the girl,

392
00:26:13,948 --> 00:26:15,324
it ruins it.

393
00:26:15,449 --> 00:26:17,118
Ah, ah.

394
00:26:18,327 --> 00:26:20,788
Okay, we'll resume shooting
in five minutes.

395
00:26:20,913 --> 00:26:21,831
Got it.

396
00:26:23,624 --> 00:26:27,211
The CEO also feels bad
about how things turned out.

397
00:26:27,336 --> 00:26:30,506
A press release about your departure
will go out once we settle.

398
00:26:30,631 --> 00:26:33,301
As for your replacement,
we're trying to find

399
00:26:33,426 --> 00:26:36,387
someone who can best match your style.

400
00:26:36,929 --> 00:26:39,348
Because of the snow scene shoot
in Daegwallyeong,

401
00:26:39,473 --> 00:26:41,225
we have to wait a month anyway,

402
00:26:41,350 --> 00:26:42,768
so there's no rush.

403
00:26:43,769 --> 00:26:46,439
Do you have any questions?

404
00:26:47,523 --> 00:26:48,983
I've been watching for 30 minutes,

405
00:26:49,108 --> 00:26:51,235
and there are
only four low-angle shots total.

406
00:26:54,697 --> 00:26:55,948
You're late.

407
00:26:56,073 --> 00:26:57,867
Why are you here?

408
00:26:58,701 --> 00:27:02,121
Because it's before Actress Song Hae-na
redid her nose.

409
00:27:02,663 --> 00:27:03,622
Aha.

410
00:27:05,124 --> 00:27:06,375
Anyway,

411
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:09,462
I didn't know you were so diligent.

412
00:27:09,587 --> 00:27:12,381
It hasn't even been two weeks
since you left the film,

413
00:27:12,506 --> 00:27:14,383
and you're already on your next one.

414
00:27:15,217 --> 00:27:16,093
It's impressive.

415
00:27:16,761 --> 00:27:20,348
I'll be in a messy court battle soon,

416
00:27:20,473 --> 00:27:21,724
and I'm dead broke.

417
00:27:22,683 --> 00:27:23,768
Ahem.

418
00:27:28,147 --> 00:27:29,065
Anything else?

419
00:27:30,733 --> 00:27:33,235
Thank you for your hard work, Director.

420
00:27:38,449 --> 00:27:40,201
Now, I'll speak as a high school friend,

421
00:27:40,326 --> 00:27:42,370
not a producer, so listen carefully.

422
00:27:44,413 --> 00:27:45,706
"Friend"?

423
00:27:45,831 --> 00:27:47,291
As an old classmate.

424
00:27:48,209 --> 00:27:52,129
I'm offering this advice
out of whatever pity I have left.

425
00:27:55,383 --> 00:27:58,135
Our lawyer will reach out
about the settlement this week.

426
00:27:58,260 --> 00:28:00,179
Don't fight it in court. Just sign it.

427
00:28:00,304 --> 00:28:01,430
No.

428
00:28:01,555 --> 00:28:04,767
Going to court
will only get messy, as you said.

429
00:28:04,892 --> 00:28:06,727
Why drag yourself through more mud?

430
00:28:06,852 --> 00:28:08,396
That's why I'm doing it.

431
00:28:10,689 --> 00:28:12,274
It's already a mess.

432
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:14,860
A little more dirt
won't change a thing for me.

433
00:28:20,825 --> 00:28:23,369
Thanks for the advice. Not that it helped.

434
00:28:49,270 --> 00:28:52,356
TWO WEEKS AGO

435
00:28:58,112 --> 00:29:00,156
Ms. Lee, we'll need high angles--

436
00:29:00,281 --> 00:29:01,115
Ms. Lee.

437
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:04,827
Ms. Song Hae-na says
she can't shoot today.

438
00:29:05,578 --> 00:29:06,412
Why not?

439
00:29:06,537 --> 00:29:09,331
She has a private brand event,

440
00:29:09,457 --> 00:29:11,417
and her manager forgot about it.

441
00:29:12,585 --> 00:29:13,419
Unbelievable.

442
00:29:16,964 --> 00:29:19,008
What? What is it?

443
00:29:22,720 --> 00:29:24,221
Ms. Lee, wait.

444
00:29:24,346 --> 00:29:25,764
Hold on.

445
00:29:27,558 --> 00:29:29,643
Allison Matin D Series.

446
00:29:29,768 --> 00:29:31,896
Para Philippe. A Louis Vucci suit.

447
00:29:32,021 --> 00:29:34,064
Cheongdam Louvacity Wine Bar.

448
00:29:34,190 --> 00:29:36,942
Height between 180 and 185 centimeters.

449
00:29:37,067 --> 00:29:39,278
The date was Wednesday, October 14th.

450
00:29:39,403 --> 00:29:42,448
That was the exact day Hae-na canceled,
claiming she had the flu.

451
00:29:43,532 --> 00:29:44,825
Should I go on?

452
00:29:56,128 --> 00:29:58,297
I told the assistant director.

453
00:29:58,923 --> 00:30:00,799
My photocall got moved up.

454
00:30:00,925 --> 00:30:04,512
You've been a no-show
seven times out of 22 shooting days.

455
00:30:04,637 --> 00:30:05,846
Ms. Lee.

456
00:30:06,764 --> 00:30:08,390
You keep changing the storyboards,

457
00:30:08,516 --> 00:30:11,018
lines, and even the shot list
on set, right?

458
00:30:12,061 --> 00:30:14,897
I tried to be understanding
since you're a rookie,

459
00:30:15,606 --> 00:30:19,068
but when the call sheet
constantly differs from the actual shoot,

460
00:30:19,193 --> 00:30:20,903
it confuses the actors.

461
00:30:21,779 --> 00:30:25,407
I figured you needed more time,

462
00:30:26,283 --> 00:30:27,826
and if I told you directly,

463
00:30:27,952 --> 00:30:31,872
I thought it'd put you on the spot,
so I was being considerate,

464
00:30:31,997 --> 00:30:33,582
but it caused a misunderstanding.

465
00:30:33,707 --> 00:30:35,501
So you did that for me?

466
00:30:35,626 --> 00:30:37,920
I'm working with a rookie director.

467
00:30:38,045 --> 00:30:40,297
This much hassle
comes with the territory, I suppose.

468
00:30:40,422 --> 00:30:43,425
The wire setup at the tank
looked unsafe earlier.

469
00:30:44,218 --> 00:30:46,303
How can I risk my life

470
00:30:46,428 --> 00:30:47,972
on such a sloppy set?

471
00:30:48,097 --> 00:30:50,808
We double-set the main wires,

472
00:30:50,933 --> 00:30:52,935
and brought in auto-braking gear

473
00:30:53,060 --> 00:30:55,354
to adjust the tension
based on water depth.

474
00:30:56,772 --> 00:30:59,400
The harness was fitted to your weight

475
00:30:59,525 --> 00:31:01,443
down to 0.1 kg.

476
00:31:02,945 --> 00:31:04,738
The water temperature is 24 degrees,

477
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:06,740
the tank pressure is normal,

478
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:08,826
and two safety divers are also on standby.

479
00:31:08,951 --> 00:31:09,785
Satisfied?

480
00:31:10,578 --> 00:31:11,412
Block them.

481
00:31:11,537 --> 00:31:12,830
-Ms. Lee.
-Stop right there.

482
00:31:12,955 --> 00:31:14,123
You can't go in.

483
00:31:14,248 --> 00:31:16,125
We have to film today!

484
00:31:18,377 --> 00:31:21,088
Let's get ready. Rolling in five.

485
00:31:22,673 --> 00:31:25,259
I said you can't go in!

486
00:31:25,384 --> 00:31:27,428
Please calm down. First…

487
00:31:32,099 --> 00:31:33,559
Are you crazy?

488
00:31:33,684 --> 00:31:35,686
You're doing this on purpose, aren't you?

489
00:31:35,811 --> 00:31:37,896
I won't let today slide.

490
00:31:39,356 --> 00:31:41,650
He's a married man, right?

491
00:31:42,610 --> 00:31:45,154
Strange how he was more careful
than an actress.

492
00:31:45,279 --> 00:31:47,906
He even switched cars twice
on the way.

493
00:31:49,199 --> 00:31:52,036
Your last-minute cancellations
were tailored to his schedule.

494
00:31:52,161 --> 00:31:53,245
Always on a weekday.

495
00:31:54,163 --> 00:31:55,289
Every Monday,

496
00:31:55,414 --> 00:31:57,249
you were always in terrible shape.

497
00:31:57,374 --> 00:31:58,959
Super hysterical.

498
00:31:59,084 --> 00:32:01,003
Have you been tailing me?

499
00:32:01,128 --> 00:32:01,962
Yes.

500
00:32:02,755 --> 00:32:04,214
And this is blackmail.

501
00:32:09,637 --> 00:32:12,097
This movie might be
just another gig to you,

502
00:32:12,806 --> 00:32:13,849
but not to me.

503
00:32:14,892 --> 00:32:16,560
I fought for this chance.

504
00:32:17,227 --> 00:32:19,813
I'm working like my life depends on it.

505
00:32:20,522 --> 00:32:22,316
It's do or die for me.

506
00:32:26,028 --> 00:32:28,614
Unless you want your life ruined
over a married guy,

507
00:32:29,448 --> 00:32:31,116
you'd better cooperate.

508
00:32:32,242 --> 00:32:33,911
Because I don't know what I'll do.

509
00:32:36,914 --> 00:32:39,291
Let's get Hae-na ready in her harness.

510
00:32:39,416 --> 00:32:40,292
Okay.

511
00:32:50,678 --> 00:32:52,721
-Make sure it's secure.
-Will do.

512
00:32:54,223 --> 00:32:55,516
Ms. Lee.

513
00:33:07,653 --> 00:33:10,989
Are you that scared of your life ending?

514
00:33:12,741 --> 00:33:14,451
Then I should end it for you.

515
00:33:15,285 --> 00:33:16,912
Your life, I mean.

516
00:34:03,792 --> 00:34:05,669
Yeong-do says
we're out of booze, so hurry.

517
00:34:05,794 --> 00:34:07,629
Where are you? I'll pick you up.

518
00:34:12,092 --> 00:34:14,428
Now this is what it's all about!

519
00:34:16,805 --> 00:34:17,973
You scared me.

520
00:34:19,183 --> 00:34:21,894
Wha… What?

521
00:34:26,523 --> 00:34:28,358
The street lighting is terrible.

522
00:34:28,484 --> 00:34:30,402
Top-down lighting ruins everything.

523
00:34:32,112 --> 00:34:34,990
I saw some of your videos.
You have an eye for composition.

524
00:34:35,657 --> 00:34:37,493
The problem is you have no taste.

525
00:34:37,618 --> 00:34:39,119
Whatever.

526
00:34:39,244 --> 00:34:40,704
It's just a hobby.

527
00:34:41,413 --> 00:34:43,165
I'll probably quit after a few.

528
00:34:43,957 --> 00:34:46,627
You get your lying from your mom,

529
00:34:46,752 --> 00:34:48,670
and your lack of skill from your dad.

530
00:34:48,796 --> 00:34:51,715
People are trashing me
saying I take after you, Auntie.

531
00:34:51,840 --> 00:34:52,883
Whatever.

532
00:34:53,842 --> 00:34:54,802
Auntie.

533
00:34:55,928 --> 00:34:58,180
Were you a bully in kindergarten?

534
00:34:58,305 --> 00:35:01,642
Ah, Lee Mi-do got kicked out
of kindergarten.

535
00:35:01,767 --> 00:35:04,144
-Twice, actually.
-Oh, come on.

536
00:35:04,269 --> 00:35:07,105
You know she carries trash around
in her sleeves, right?

537
00:35:07,731 --> 00:35:09,566
Emptying it for her is weirdly satisfying.

538
00:35:10,484 --> 00:35:13,111
Oh, right. She wore the same socks
for three days once.

539
00:35:13,237 --> 00:35:14,071
I saw it.

540
00:35:14,196 --> 00:35:15,405
-You saw it, right?
-Yeah.

541
00:35:15,531 --> 00:35:16,490
She still does.

542
00:35:16,615 --> 00:35:17,658
Four days tops, though.

543
00:35:17,783 --> 00:35:19,368
And you're still marrying her?

544
00:35:19,493 --> 00:35:20,994
Knowing all that?

545
00:35:22,454 --> 00:35:24,122
Snap out of it, Namgung!

546
00:35:24,248 --> 00:35:25,332
Hey.

547
00:35:25,457 --> 00:35:26,458
Give it up.

548
00:35:26,583 --> 00:35:29,753
He has already heard 72 of her flaws
and still takes her side.

549
00:35:30,420 --> 00:35:32,172
That's true love, you know?

550
00:35:36,385 --> 00:35:39,805
Hey, rather than marrying Lee Mi-do,
just become a monk.

551
00:35:41,014 --> 00:35:42,850
Don't say that in front of her.

552
00:35:42,975 --> 00:35:44,977
She acts tough, but gets hurt easily.

553
00:35:45,102 --> 00:35:47,437
-She brought it on herself.
-Watch it.

554
00:35:51,066 --> 00:35:52,192
Hey.

555
00:35:52,317 --> 00:35:55,279
Does your heart still flutter
when you see Lee Mi-do?

556
00:35:55,404 --> 00:35:57,739
Does it go pitter-patter?

557
00:36:04,663 --> 00:36:07,124
Yeah, it still flutters.

558
00:36:08,250 --> 00:36:11,920
I miss her when she's not around,
and I feel empty without her.

559
00:36:12,045 --> 00:36:14,464
Even if we're together 24/7,
I never get sick of her.

560
00:36:14,590 --> 00:36:17,009
If anything, time goes by too fast.

561
00:36:17,926 --> 00:36:19,136
How is this possible?

562
00:36:19,761 --> 00:36:21,221
Honestly, it amazes me too.

563
00:36:25,017 --> 00:36:26,894
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

564
00:36:35,569 --> 00:36:36,486
Mr. Eom.

565
00:36:37,863 --> 00:36:40,449
How could you
stab me in the back like this?

566
00:36:42,034 --> 00:36:43,744
What is your reason?

567
00:36:43,869 --> 00:36:45,746
We already agreed
to postpone the schedule.

568
00:36:47,497 --> 00:36:51,335
Option one, you chickened out of asking
General Manager Kang for a delay.

569
00:36:51,919 --> 00:36:55,213
Option two, you chickened out of trying
to meet the year-end pop-up schedule.

570
00:36:55,339 --> 00:36:56,298
Option three,

571
00:36:57,049 --> 00:36:57,883
you chickened out

572
00:36:58,008 --> 00:37:00,677
because TF Snack Teams 1 and 5's products
launch next month.

573
00:37:02,721 --> 00:37:04,932
Tell me which one it is.

574
00:37:05,057 --> 00:37:06,600
-So I can--
-Option four.

575
00:37:07,684 --> 00:37:11,605
He chickened out because the sample
from TF Snack Team 5 was high quality.

576
00:37:16,735 --> 00:37:19,071
Oh, I'm sorry.

577
00:37:20,072 --> 00:37:21,615
I thought you were my manager.

578
00:37:26,578 --> 00:37:27,537
I apologize.

579
00:37:37,089 --> 00:37:39,591
There's no way
Team 5's sample was that good.

580
00:37:41,468 --> 00:37:43,345
Yesterday's sample actually was.

581
00:37:43,887 --> 00:37:46,431
-Yesterday's?
-We share R&D, so I've tried it.

582
00:37:46,556 --> 00:37:49,685
They fixed the sweet and salty balance

583
00:37:49,810 --> 00:37:51,061
that was lacking before.

584
00:37:52,187 --> 00:37:54,606
I mean, nice aftertaste,

585
00:37:54,731 --> 00:37:56,441
and a rich flavor.

586
00:37:57,859 --> 00:38:00,278
It'll probably beat
your team's internal survey scores.

587
00:38:02,739 --> 00:38:03,657
Hmm.

588
00:38:04,658 --> 00:38:06,868
So you're the one who wrote,
"My condolences."

589
00:38:08,662 --> 00:38:10,956
I'm Park Su-a from Snack Team 4.

590
00:38:11,707 --> 00:38:13,542
You're Assistant Manager Namgung Ho

591
00:38:14,334 --> 00:38:15,961
from TF Snack Team 3, right?

592
00:38:19,548 --> 00:38:22,050
I know the reason why

593
00:38:23,260 --> 00:38:24,511
the fourth sample had issues.

594
00:38:25,512 --> 00:38:26,722
Want me to tell you?

595
00:38:39,359 --> 00:38:41,069
DIRECTOR OH GYEONG-SU'S
MONUMENTAL MASTERPIECE SET IN FLORENCE

596
00:38:41,194 --> 00:38:42,112
WHEN THAT DAY COMES

597
00:38:47,826 --> 00:38:50,829
INCOMING CALL

598
00:38:54,541 --> 00:38:55,876
Nice to meet you.

599
00:38:56,001 --> 00:38:58,837
I'm Han Tae-seung, attorney for Nobu Film.

600
00:39:04,259 --> 00:39:06,511
This is our draft of the settlement.

601
00:39:06,636 --> 00:39:08,722
Thought we'd put this on the table first.

602
00:39:09,723 --> 00:39:10,599
SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT

603
00:39:10,724 --> 00:39:11,725
Take a look,

604
00:39:12,267 --> 00:39:15,479
and let me know
if you have any questions or revisions.

605
00:39:19,608 --> 00:39:22,069
No full payment of the directing fee,

606
00:39:23,111 --> 00:39:24,905
and a 3% copyright stake?

607
00:39:25,030 --> 00:39:28,116
Since the fault lies on your end,

608
00:39:28,241 --> 00:39:29,868
we ask for your understanding.

609
00:39:29,993 --> 00:39:31,411
I can't accept this.

610
00:39:33,997 --> 00:39:35,874
Because you forced the shoot,

611
00:39:35,999 --> 00:39:38,043
Ms. Song Hae-na got injured.

612
00:39:38,168 --> 00:39:41,254
She's still suffering from mental distress

613
00:39:41,379 --> 00:39:42,881
and is refusing to film.

614
00:39:44,299 --> 00:39:46,885
So you are clearly at fault here.

615
00:39:48,553 --> 00:39:51,264
You make it sound like
she broke a limb or something.

616
00:39:51,389 --> 00:39:52,516
Above all, your exit

617
00:39:52,641 --> 00:39:55,060
cost the production company
more than expected.

618
00:39:55,185 --> 00:39:58,855
Counting the wages of over 40 staff
over the two-month delay

619
00:39:58,980 --> 00:40:00,816
and the set rental fees alone,

620
00:40:00,941 --> 00:40:02,317
it's over 300 million won.

621
00:40:06,571 --> 00:40:09,574
What happens if I don't agree
to this settlement?

622
00:40:09,699 --> 00:40:11,910
I can't say for sure,

623
00:40:12,619 --> 00:40:13,954
but maybe around next month,

624
00:40:14,079 --> 00:40:16,498
"Director Lee Mi-do
dismissed from  Heartless

625
00:40:16,623 --> 00:40:18,375
due to incompetence"

626
00:40:18,500 --> 00:40:20,043
will be the headline.

627
00:40:21,378 --> 00:40:22,754
But if you agree,

628
00:40:22,879 --> 00:40:25,507
"Director Lee Mi-do
steps down from  Heartless…

629
00:40:27,676 --> 00:40:29,594
due to health reasons"

630
00:40:30,428 --> 00:40:32,097
is what the article will say.

631
00:40:32,222 --> 00:40:34,474
The choice is entirely yours.

632
00:40:35,183 --> 00:40:37,185
But I can't give you much time,

633
00:40:37,894 --> 00:40:40,438
so by next week at the latest--

634
00:40:47,988 --> 00:40:48,822
What is it?

635
00:40:49,489 --> 00:40:50,448
Is something wrong?

636
00:40:50,574 --> 00:40:53,368
No, I came in because you rang the bell.

637
00:40:53,493 --> 00:40:54,452
Didn't you?

638
00:40:54,578 --> 00:40:55,871
The bell?

639
00:40:55,996 --> 00:40:57,038
I rang it.

640
00:40:57,164 --> 00:40:58,957
Mind if I order something?

641
00:41:04,838 --> 00:41:07,632
One bottle of Ravelo 4500,

642
00:41:07,757 --> 00:41:09,050
a fruit platter,

643
00:41:09,176 --> 00:41:11,303
and ice and sparkling water, please.

644
00:41:11,970 --> 00:41:13,847
Sure, I'll bring them right away.

645
00:41:15,640 --> 00:41:18,185
I'll send the finalized settlement
next week.

646
00:41:18,310 --> 00:41:20,187
You seem busy. You can go.

647
00:41:29,613 --> 00:41:33,158
You remember Chairman Choi's case
from last year, right?

648
00:41:33,825 --> 00:41:36,286
The prosecution argued intent
back then too,

649
00:41:36,953 --> 00:41:38,830
but we got an acquittal.

650
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:41,541
Leave this to me,

651
00:41:41,666 --> 00:41:43,418
and focus on your next project.

652
00:41:45,253 --> 00:41:46,171
Yes?

653
00:41:56,556 --> 00:41:58,725
So how many bottles have gone in?

654
00:41:58,850 --> 00:42:02,103
Two 21-year Monterios, one 30-year,
and the first bottle of Ravelo.

655
00:42:02,229 --> 00:42:04,314
-Don't blame me
-Me!

656
00:42:04,439 --> 00:42:05,982
-For being
-Being!

657
00:42:06,149 --> 00:42:09,444
So cruel

658
00:42:10,278 --> 00:42:16,409
-I chose to walk away for your sake
-I chose to walk away for your sake

659
00:42:16,534 --> 00:42:18,286
-Don't forget
-Don't forget

660
00:42:18,411 --> 00:42:20,497
-My love
-Love!

661
00:42:20,622 --> 00:42:22,249
You're inside my…

662
00:42:25,210 --> 00:42:26,253
What do we do?

663
00:42:28,880 --> 00:42:30,423
Don't take any more orders.

664
00:42:31,174 --> 00:42:32,050
Yes, sir.

665
00:42:39,140 --> 00:42:40,642
What a total nutjob.

666
00:42:49,025 --> 00:42:51,152
Ms. Lee, are you going to
sign the settlement?

667
00:42:51,278 --> 00:42:53,238
Are you crazy? Why would she?

668
00:42:53,363 --> 00:42:56,658
Still, we need to expose this tyranny

669
00:42:56,783 --> 00:42:58,952
from the studio and the actor.

670
00:42:59,077 --> 00:43:01,204
Hey, if this gets out of hand,

671
00:43:01,329 --> 00:43:02,998
it'll only make things harder for her!

672
00:43:03,123 --> 00:43:05,000
-Shut up, you're loud.
-Why?

673
00:43:05,125 --> 00:43:06,042
Everyone, stop.

674
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:07,419
You guys,

675
00:43:08,128 --> 00:43:09,963
don't come to the motel starting tomorrow.

676
00:43:10,088 --> 00:43:11,840
That's why I called you here.

677
00:43:12,716 --> 00:43:15,468
I only brought you in temporarily
because we were short-staffed.

678
00:43:15,593 --> 00:43:17,679
I never meant to keep you.

679
00:43:17,804 --> 00:43:19,681
Director Gong Ji-min is starting a movie,

680
00:43:19,806 --> 00:43:22,267
so I asked him to hire you three.

681
00:43:22,392 --> 00:43:25,353
Go and do a good job, okay?
Don't embarrass me.

682
00:43:25,895 --> 00:43:27,480
No way.

683
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:30,191
I want to keep working with you.

684
00:43:30,317 --> 00:43:32,861
Lee Guk-jin, stop whining.

685
00:43:32,986 --> 00:43:35,530
If you have time for that,
write another line.

686
00:43:36,072 --> 00:43:37,324
Off you go. Get up.

687
00:43:43,663 --> 00:43:44,497
Huh?

688
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:46,541
Babe.

689
00:44:00,638 --> 00:44:03,558
How did you know they were there?

690
00:44:03,683 --> 00:44:05,977
They practically flaunted it
on social media.

691
00:44:06,102 --> 00:44:07,937
So you saw the post and went.

692
00:44:08,063 --> 00:44:10,106
-Who threw the first punch?
-This jerk.

693
00:44:10,231 --> 00:44:11,399
He just lunged at me!

694
00:44:11,524 --> 00:44:13,943
She cheated on me!
How could I not be mad?

695
00:44:14,069 --> 00:44:16,488
I've told you so many times that's not it!

696
00:44:16,613 --> 00:44:17,614
Hey!

697
00:44:18,531 --> 00:44:19,991
As if you did nothing wrong!

698
00:44:20,116 --> 00:44:21,743
That's enough already.

699
00:44:23,036 --> 00:44:24,829
This is all because of you.

700
00:44:24,954 --> 00:44:27,457
Fired from your own movie
and shooting porn.

701
00:44:27,582 --> 00:44:28,917
Have some shame!

702
00:44:29,042 --> 00:44:31,753
Why bring her into that mess as crew?

703
00:44:31,878 --> 00:44:33,963
Ruin your own life if you want to.

704
00:44:34,089 --> 00:44:36,508
Shooting an adult film isn't embarrassing.

705
00:44:36,633 --> 00:44:38,468
What's embarrassing is your behavior.

706
00:44:39,260 --> 00:44:41,137
And you're not helping Jang-mi.

707
00:44:41,262 --> 00:44:42,097
What?

708
00:44:42,222 --> 00:44:44,099
Are you out of your damn mind?

709
00:44:45,225 --> 00:44:46,893
What the hell?

710
00:45:05,245 --> 00:45:07,080
Sorry I didn't tell you sooner.

711
00:45:07,789 --> 00:45:08,957
Let me explain.

712
00:45:11,376 --> 00:45:13,420
I heard it all. What's left to explain?

713
00:45:14,254 --> 00:45:16,673
Song Hae-na went on a power trip,
and you snapped again, right?

714
00:45:16,798 --> 00:45:18,508
And you needed money for legal fees,

715
00:45:18,633 --> 00:45:21,678
so you broke your promise
and shot an adult film. Am I wrong?

716
00:45:22,512 --> 00:45:23,513
I'm sorry.

717
00:45:24,347 --> 00:45:25,432
Oh Yeon-ju's the producer?

718
00:45:28,726 --> 00:45:30,645
Are you crazy? What are you doing?

719
00:45:31,396 --> 00:45:33,273
You said there's no new director yet.

720
00:45:33,398 --> 00:45:34,774
You still have a chance.

721
00:45:44,117 --> 00:45:46,786
If it fails again,
how will you face your mom?

722
00:45:47,912 --> 00:45:49,998
What will you tell people this time?

723
00:45:50,748 --> 00:45:53,751
How will you lie to yourself
and pretend you're fine?

724
00:45:53,877 --> 00:45:55,295
You're not fine.

725
00:45:55,837 --> 00:45:56,921
You won't be fine.

726
00:45:57,046 --> 00:45:59,841
You said you didn't care if it flopped.

727
00:45:59,966 --> 00:46:02,385
What about you? Do you think it's fine?

728
00:46:02,927 --> 00:46:04,095
Do you not care?

729
00:46:05,305 --> 00:46:09,017
Why should you listen to people
who say your life is ruined?

730
00:46:10,477 --> 00:46:12,270
I made myself clear.

731
00:46:13,354 --> 00:46:14,439
To do your best.

732
00:46:15,190 --> 00:46:16,191
To have no regrets.

733
00:46:17,233 --> 00:46:18,776
But that's not what you're doing.

734
00:46:18,902 --> 00:46:20,945
You'll regret it. I know you will.

735
00:46:22,864 --> 00:46:23,823
This is my problem.

736
00:46:25,325 --> 00:46:26,284
I'll handle it.

737
00:46:26,409 --> 00:46:27,577
Stop interfering.

738
00:46:27,702 --> 00:46:30,038
Then don't make me worry!

739
00:46:37,879 --> 00:46:39,839
Look where handling it got you!

740
00:46:40,507 --> 00:46:41,925
That's as far as you got.

741
00:46:42,509 --> 00:46:43,968
How can I just stand by?

742
00:46:44,093 --> 00:46:45,762
You should have told me first,

743
00:46:45,887 --> 00:46:48,431
-so I could help--
-I didn't want you to know!

744
00:46:50,475 --> 00:46:53,186
I'd rather die
than have you see me like this.

745
00:46:55,688 --> 00:46:57,649
It feels even more pathetic
than I thought.

746
00:47:01,361 --> 00:47:02,362
Ah.

747
00:47:04,239 --> 00:47:05,949
So this is how it feels.

748
00:47:33,851 --> 00:47:35,019
Let's talk for a second.

749
00:47:39,232 --> 00:47:40,567
Earlier, I was…

750
00:47:40,692 --> 00:47:42,402
Let's break up.

751
00:47:46,447 --> 00:47:47,365
Hey, Lee Mi-do.

752
00:47:47,490 --> 00:47:49,576
We should end it here.

753
00:47:54,747 --> 00:47:56,291
Look, I was wrong earlier.

754
00:47:58,084 --> 00:48:00,336
I shouldn't have spoken to you like that.

755
00:48:01,546 --> 00:48:03,631
I only thought about my own feelings.

756
00:48:03,756 --> 00:48:05,008
I'm sorry.

757
00:48:05,133 --> 00:48:06,342
When did that start?

758
00:48:08,428 --> 00:48:11,431
You said I was
your driving force and compass.

759
00:48:11,556 --> 00:48:12,599
Since when?

760
00:48:15,643 --> 00:48:17,145
Yeah, it still flutters.

761
00:48:18,021 --> 00:48:19,314
How is this possible?

762
00:48:19,856 --> 00:48:21,107
Honestly, it amazes me too.

763
00:48:23,484 --> 00:48:25,945
That's what I'd love to say,
but it's not true.

764
00:48:26,070 --> 00:48:27,322
I almost believed you.

765
00:48:27,447 --> 00:48:29,741
What, so you don't get
butterflies anymore?

766
00:48:29,866 --> 00:48:31,618
It's been ten years with Lee Mi-do.

767
00:48:31,743 --> 00:48:33,411
It'd be weird if I still did.

768
00:48:36,080 --> 00:48:37,415
To me, Lee Mi-do is

769
00:48:38,291 --> 00:48:40,084
my motivation to stay at my job

770
00:48:40,960 --> 00:48:42,587
and my life's compass.

771
00:48:44,297 --> 00:48:46,758
Every time I want to quit my job,

772
00:48:46,883 --> 00:48:48,718
she's what keeps me holding on.

773
00:48:51,262 --> 00:48:53,014
She's the compass

774
00:48:53,723 --> 00:48:56,684
that keeps me from straying off track.

775
00:48:59,562 --> 00:49:02,440
Just got to endure it for 30 years
and it's over, right?

776
00:49:04,692 --> 00:49:06,277
I can't wait to grow old.

777
00:49:14,952 --> 00:49:16,746
I'm a heavy burden to you.

778
00:49:17,413 --> 00:49:18,581
I bet it's overwhelming.

779
00:49:19,707 --> 00:49:21,584
So let's just stop.

780
00:49:21,709 --> 00:49:23,002
Hey, Mi-do.

781
00:49:24,504 --> 00:49:25,922
It's not like that.

782
00:49:26,047 --> 00:49:27,256
That's not what I meant.

783
00:49:29,008 --> 00:49:31,260
You know how I really feel.

784
00:49:33,429 --> 00:49:35,390
You don't get butterflies anymore, do you?

785
00:49:36,265 --> 00:49:37,558
You said so yourself.

786
00:49:38,810 --> 00:49:41,396
That I always made
your heart race out of control.

787
00:49:41,521 --> 00:49:42,980
Do you still feel that way?

788
00:49:43,106 --> 00:49:44,023
You don't, right?

789
00:49:44,941 --> 00:49:46,734
It's been ten years, Mi-do.

790
00:49:47,318 --> 00:49:48,820
The rush can't last forever.

791
00:49:49,862 --> 00:49:50,905
Namgung.

792
00:49:51,781 --> 00:49:54,200
You didn't think I was heavy
in middle school

793
00:49:54,325 --> 00:49:56,577
because that's how much you loved me.

794
00:50:03,042 --> 00:50:04,919
So what are you trying to say?

795
00:50:06,879 --> 00:50:09,507
We're not like that anymore,
so we should break up?

796
00:50:13,886 --> 00:50:14,887
Fine.

797
00:50:16,639 --> 00:50:18,391
You're right. We're not like before.

798
00:50:18,516 --> 00:50:19,475
But still,

799
00:50:20,351 --> 00:50:22,979
that doesn't erase our time together

800
00:50:23,104 --> 00:50:25,273
or mean we don't love each other.
It's just…

801
00:50:26,524 --> 00:50:29,485
something that every couple goes through.
The rush can't last forever.

802
00:50:34,782 --> 00:50:35,992
I'll try harder.

803
00:50:41,122 --> 00:50:41,956
Mi-do.

804
00:50:44,250 --> 00:50:47,712
I think I've been neglecting you.

805
00:50:50,506 --> 00:50:52,884
I'll try twice, three times as hard--

806
00:50:53,009 --> 00:50:55,178
And I'll become
that much more of a burden.

807
00:50:57,305 --> 00:50:59,098
And I'll feel even more pathetic.

808
00:51:06,439 --> 00:51:07,398
Namgung.

809
00:51:09,484 --> 00:51:11,110
Your love…

810
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:16,157
No, your sense of responsibility,
obligation, and guilt

811
00:51:17,617 --> 00:51:19,118
makes me feel pathetic.

812
00:51:22,038 --> 00:51:23,998
It makes me hate myself more and more.

813
00:51:26,000 --> 00:51:27,126
What?

814
00:51:27,251 --> 00:51:28,377
You know what?

815
00:51:29,295 --> 00:51:31,130
I'm always walking on eggshells
around you.

816
00:51:32,924 --> 00:51:34,175
You see,

817
00:51:34,300 --> 00:51:36,552
walking on eggshells
and being considerate seem similar.

818
00:51:36,677 --> 00:51:37,553
But…

819
00:51:38,387 --> 00:51:41,390
Being considerate
makes me feel like a better person.

820
00:51:43,684 --> 00:51:46,354
But walking on eggshells
just makes me feel pathetic.

821
00:51:50,233 --> 00:51:53,110
And if I feel any more pathetic,
I'll be done for good.

822
00:51:54,821 --> 00:51:55,738
Mm-hmm.

823
00:51:59,867 --> 00:52:01,869
So let's break up.

824
00:52:05,206 --> 00:52:07,375
I make you feel pathetic?

825
00:52:17,593 --> 00:52:19,554
Do you really want to break up?

826
00:52:23,766 --> 00:52:24,642
Yes.

827
00:52:25,184 --> 00:52:26,894
Is that really what you want?

828
00:52:35,444 --> 00:52:36,946
I'll ask you one last time.

829
00:52:38,990 --> 00:52:40,074
Think carefully.

830
00:52:43,661 --> 00:52:45,371
Do you really want to break up?

831
00:52:47,999 --> 00:52:49,959
Yes. Let's break up.

832
00:52:56,841 --> 00:52:57,842
Okay.

833
00:53:00,553 --> 00:53:02,138
Fine, let's break up.

834
00:53:54,398 --> 00:53:56,609
LOVING YOU
WAS THE BEST THING I'VE EVER DONE

835
00:53:56,776 --> 00:53:59,403
IT'S BEEN TEN YEARS,
BUT I'M STILL GETTING TO KNOW YOU

836
00:53:59,528 --> 00:54:02,615
LET'S KEEP BEING US AND STAY TOGETHER
I LOVE YOU

837
00:54:05,826 --> 00:54:08,454
Because our time together was so radiant,

838
00:54:09,580 --> 00:54:12,041
and because it was so happy,

839
00:54:13,626 --> 00:54:15,378
I fooled myself and you

840
00:54:15,920 --> 00:54:17,505
into thinking

841
00:54:18,339 --> 00:54:21,509
it was still the same,
that nothing had changed.

842
00:54:36,065 --> 00:54:37,233
Oh…

843
00:54:39,193 --> 00:54:40,736
But we both know.

844
00:54:41,904 --> 00:54:44,573
Our love no longer sparkles.

845
00:54:48,953 --> 00:54:51,247
Our love is suffocatingly heavy.

846
00:54:52,289 --> 00:54:54,208
Withered and pathetic.

847
00:54:56,877 --> 00:54:59,005
MY BABY

848
00:55:02,842 --> 00:55:04,301
-He's not picking up?
-No.

849
00:55:06,178 --> 00:55:07,847
-He's not?
-No.

850
00:55:08,514 --> 00:55:10,266
Wait, did those two fight?

851
00:55:10,391 --> 00:55:11,308
Damn it.

852
00:55:12,059 --> 00:55:13,102
What do we do?

853
00:55:13,227 --> 00:55:14,603
What do you mean?

854
00:55:15,146 --> 00:55:16,605
Everything is set and ready.

855
00:55:18,607 --> 00:55:19,567
Try calling again.

856
00:55:19,692 --> 00:55:22,737
TO THE ONE ALWAYS BY MY SIDE

857
00:55:23,988 --> 00:55:25,197
Ugh, seriously.

858
00:55:25,322 --> 00:55:27,241
MI-DO, WILL YOU MARRY ME?

859
00:56:21,337 --> 00:56:22,338
And just like that,

860
00:56:23,255 --> 00:56:25,758
our ten-year relationship came to an end.

861
00:56:45,402 --> 00:56:46,946
NAMGUNG-TUSH

862
00:56:48,906 --> 00:56:50,116
Hello?

863
00:56:50,783 --> 00:56:52,827
Wake up, Lee Mi-do.

864
00:56:52,952 --> 00:56:55,371
Mmm, I'm getting up.

865
00:56:56,497 --> 00:56:58,582
I love you, love you, mwah.

866
00:56:59,291 --> 00:57:02,503
Me too. I love you, love you, mwah.

867
00:57:24,400 --> 00:57:25,234
Oh!

868
00:57:44,128 --> 00:57:45,129
Oh? It's snowing.

869
00:57:45,254 --> 00:57:46,338
SHORT FILM SCREENING

870
00:57:46,463 --> 00:57:49,049
Wow, they said
we'd get our first snow today.

871
00:57:49,175 --> 00:57:50,551
The Liar Agency was actually right.

872
00:57:51,302 --> 00:57:52,469
DIRECTOR LEE MI-DO

873
00:57:54,013 --> 00:57:55,514
LOOKING FORWARD TO YOUR NEXT FILM

874
00:57:55,639 --> 00:57:56,932
WISHING YOU GOOD HEALTH

875
00:57:57,850 --> 00:58:00,519
Did you happen to see who wrote this?

876
00:58:01,687 --> 00:58:02,980
Umm…

877
00:58:03,105 --> 00:58:05,274
He just walked out a moment ago.

878
00:58:07,276 --> 00:58:09,486
Ms. Lee, your interview starts soon.

879
00:58:09,612 --> 00:58:10,487
Ms. Lee!

880
00:58:13,824 --> 00:58:16,202
AFTER SPRING COMES WINTER

881
00:58:24,043 --> 00:58:26,003
Namgung is leaving for Australia today.

882
00:58:26,128 --> 00:58:27,838
You know his older friend from college

883
00:58:27,963 --> 00:58:29,715
who runs a big Korean restaurant there.

884
00:58:30,674 --> 00:58:32,760
He asked Namgung
to go into business with him.

885
00:58:35,221 --> 00:58:37,681
He said he's so done
being friends with you.

886
00:58:38,807 --> 00:58:40,684
He's sick and tired of you.

887
00:58:40,809 --> 00:58:42,561
He even hates Korea because of you.

888
00:58:45,231 --> 00:58:47,441
He'll come back once he gets over you.

889
00:59:00,913 --> 00:59:06,210
The next buses are 6716, 603…

890
00:59:19,056 --> 00:59:20,182
You can chase me,

891
00:59:21,225 --> 00:59:22,726
but don't stop halfway.

892
00:59:25,938 --> 00:59:27,481
Lee Mi-do, you…

893
00:59:28,440 --> 00:59:29,858
never come to me

894
00:59:31,193 --> 00:59:32,820
if I don't come to you first.

895
00:59:34,280 --> 00:59:36,073
You said you're done being my friend.

896
00:59:36,615 --> 00:59:37,574
That's right.

897
00:59:39,034 --> 00:59:40,077
I'm done.

898
00:59:41,787 --> 00:59:43,747
You're so high-maintenance. I can't.

899
00:59:49,378 --> 00:59:51,380
I know what you're afraid of.

900
00:59:54,300 --> 00:59:55,968
Because I was terrified too.

901
00:59:57,720 --> 00:59:58,637
But…

902
00:59:59,847 --> 01:00:01,140
but Mi-do…

903
01:00:03,309 --> 01:00:05,185
What you're worried about won't happen.

904
01:00:08,272 --> 01:00:10,274
That cliché routine
of dating and breaking up…

905
01:00:12,693 --> 01:00:13,944
won't happen to us.

906
01:00:16,280 --> 01:00:17,614
How can you be sure?

907
01:00:20,159 --> 01:00:22,036
Because I love you so much.

908
01:00:27,207 --> 01:00:29,001
More than you think.

909
01:00:31,003 --> 01:00:33,005
So much that even I can't handle it.

910
01:00:36,675 --> 01:00:38,093
I love you so much.

911
01:01:09,500 --> 01:01:11,919
The day we went from friends to lovers,

912
01:01:12,544 --> 01:01:14,129
the first snow fell in Seoul.

913
01:01:15,381 --> 01:01:18,092
After that, our anniversary
wasn't a specific date,

914
01:01:18,717 --> 01:01:21,136
but the day the first snow fell in Seoul.

915
01:01:22,346 --> 01:01:25,265
We welcomed nine first snows together,

916
01:01:26,100 --> 01:01:27,810
madly in love.

917
01:01:29,144 --> 01:01:31,271
And before the tenth,

918
01:01:32,481 --> 01:01:33,941
we broke up.

919
01:01:53,001 --> 01:01:55,254
THANK YOU TO OH DONG-MIN
FOR HIS SPECIAL APPEARANCE

920
01:01:57,840 --> 01:01:59,591
You're going to make up anyway.

921
01:01:59,716 --> 01:02:02,136
Aren't you worried about Lee Mi-do?

922
01:02:02,261 --> 01:02:03,971
I told you I broke up with her.

923
01:02:04,096 --> 01:02:05,055
We split it 50-50.

924
01:02:05,180 --> 01:02:06,807
-Don't change your mind later.
-You too.

925
01:02:06,974 --> 01:02:09,309
The Spicy SweeTato Chips were the worst.

926
01:02:09,476 --> 01:02:10,436
I smoke those, too.

927
01:02:10,561 --> 01:02:12,646
The person who got me smoking
in high school smoked those.

928
01:02:13,772 --> 01:02:15,149
Show up like this again and you're dead.

929
01:02:15,274 --> 01:02:17,067
Since you want it so badly,
I'll see you in court.

930
01:02:17,734 --> 01:02:19,736
-What is it this time?
-Just don't worry about it!

931
01:02:19,862 --> 01:02:21,363
But I can't help it.

932
01:02:21,989 --> 01:02:25,534
The passion we had back then…
the butterflies…

933
01:02:26,410 --> 01:02:28,412
where did it all go?

934
01:02:29,079 --> 01:02:31,039
Translation by Soya Back
